        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8049d9f0-991b-5f7c-b516-628b39c42a47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Tarawa, Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River\n- Organizations: Eighth Army Ranger Company\n- Places: Ch'ongch'on River Valley, North Korea\n- Topics: Korean War, World War II, Pacific Theater\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Tarawa was fought in the Pacific Theater of World War II from 20 to 23 November 1943.\n- The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River was a decisive battle in the Korean War fought from 25 November to 2 December 1950 along the Ch'ongch'on River Valley in northwestern North Korea.\n- The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River was also known as the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on and the Second Phase Campaign Western Sector.\n- The Eighth Army Ranger Company was best known for defending Hill 205 against an overwhelming Chinese attack during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River.\n- The defense of Hill 205 during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River resulted in 41 of the 51 Rangers in the Eighth Army Ranger Company becoming casualties.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "75f63dde-960e-5da6-b8d6-f871f69b91bf",
        "text": "Page: Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River. Sentence: The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River, also known as the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on () or the Second Phase Campaign Western Sector (), was a decisive battle in the Korean War, and it took place from November 25 to December 2, 1950, along the Ch'ongch'on River Valley in the northwestern part of North Korea.\nPage: Battle of Tarawa. Sentence: The Battle of Tarawa was a battle in the Pacific Theater of World War II that was fought on 20–23 November 1943.\nPage: Eighth Army Ranger Company. Sentence: It was best known for its defense of Hill 205 against an overwhelming Chinese attack during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River which resulted 41 of the 51 Rangers becoming casualties.",
